ment building in  boulder colorado  that was built to give the homeless a  permanent place to live  where we met ray vose who builds  electric bikes in his apartment  that can sell for about eighteen hundred  dollars  oh my word these are the electric  bikes this is the current project this  is amazing  well that one there is my daily driver  right now  what was the worst night or the worst  day  that you had when you were homeless  right i was sitting in a barn  spending my last two bucks and change on  up here  it was called and you know  just remember reading stories about  freezing to death  you know it's not that painful you know  you feel warm i was considering giving  up  yeah just going out and freezing to  death yeah  now those has a place of his own here  residents sign a lease and pay rent as a  portion of any income  such as social security or disability  greg harms ceo of boulder shelter for  the homeless  lays out the rules just like anybody  else who lives in an apartment  if you're going to have your friends  over and have loud parties that's not  acceptable  right if you're going to trash your  apartment that's not acceptable  if you don't pay your rent that's not  acceptable as long as you meet the  obligations of your lease  while you're staying here you know  you're welcome to stay once  there is housing then comes dealing with  problems like  alcohol and drug abuse illness  unemployment  so there's not a requirement that you  become sober there's not a requirement  that you get on your meds there's not a  requirement that you  you find employment because what we  found is when you put those requirements  in place  then people are are inevitably not able  to  to meet one of those requirements and  their housing is in jeopardy  and that's that's not the goal the goal  is to keep them housed  what happens with my next social  security check housing first has its  critics  chief among them robert marbert jr  president trump's  executive director of 